      en: "Sangaste Castle, also known as Sagnitz, is a neo-Gothic manor in southern Estonia, built 1873-1879 for Count Friedrich von Berg. The castle's most striking feature is its 50-meter-high tower, offering panoramic views. The interior is famous for its carved woodwork and a collection of hunting trophies. The architect Robert Pohlitz designed it in the English Gothic style, with pointed arches and battlements. During the Soviet era, the castle was used as a granary, leading to some deterioration. After restoration, it opened as a luxury hotel and event venue. The surrounding park has a variety of exotic trees and a pond.",
