      en: "Kunda Manor is a neoclassical manor house in Kunda, Estonia, built in 1873 for the von Girard de Soucanton family. The two-story stone building features a central risalit and a balcony. The manor is set in a park with a pond. After nationalization, it was used as offices for the neighboring cement factory. Restoration in the 1990s converted it into a museum showcasing local history and a restaurant. The manor is surrounded by several preserved outbuildings, including a stable and a distillery.",
