      en: "Taagepera Castle, also known as Wagenfer, is an Art Nouveau manor house in Helme Parish, Estonia, built between 1910-1912 for the von Stryk family. Designed by architect Otto Wildau in the Nordic Romantic style, the castle has an irregular plan with multiple towers and turrets. The interior features painted murals, tiled stoves, and stained glass. After nationalization, it operated as a tuberculosis sanatorium. Since the 1990s, it has been a successful hotel and wellness center. The castle is surrounded by a landscaped park and is a popular wedding venue.",
