      en: "Rannu Church is a medieval Lutheran church located in the village of Rannu, Tartu County, Estonia. The area is primarily agricultural, with farms growing grains and vegetables. The church serves a congregation of about 250 members. The nearby Emajõgi River is a popular fishing spot. The church is a tourist attraction for its historic interior. The nearest town, Elva, is 15 km away. The church is part of the Estonian Evangelical Lutheran Church and is open to visitors in summer.",
